(1, 1, 1, 'How can we make a 3-day Manipur trip useful for a family visiting from Delhi?”', 'Hello Admin,\n\nTo make a 3-day Manipur trip highly \"useful,\" seamless, and memorable for a family visiting from Delhi, we must address their likely priorities: **convenience, comfort, safety, time optimization, and experiencing authentic Manipuri culture without logistical stress.** \n\nAs the platform administrator, you can leverage ManipurApp’s modular ecosystem to curate a hassle-free, end-to-end experience. Here is a practical strategy and a structured 3-day itinerary showing how the app’s modules can be packaged for this family.\n\n---\n\n### Phase 1: Configuring the App for the Delhi Family (Admin Setup)\n\nDelhi travelers often appreciate pre-planned, reliable packages to avoid negotiating on the ground. You can configure the following in your Admin Dashboard:\n\n1. **Create a \"3-Day Imphal & Loktak Family Package\"** in the **Tourism & Bookings Module**.\n2. **Bundle Taxi Services:** Set up dedicated flat-rate \"8-hour Local Imphal\" and \"Outstation Loktak/Moirang\" packages in the **Taxi Module**.\n3. **Curate \"Delhi-Friendly\" Dining Guides:** Highlight restaurants in the **Restaurant Module** that offer hygienic local Manipuri fine-dining (like *Meitei traditional thali*) alongside familiar Indian/Continental options for kids.\n4. **Airport Welcome Notification:** Set a geo-triggered push notification via **Member Services** for users landing at Bir Tikendrajit International Airport (IMF): *\"Welcome to Manipur! Book your certified airport transfer and local tour guide directly on ManipurApp.\"*\n\n---\n\n### Phase 2: The Recommended 3-Day Itinerary (Integrated with ManipurApp)\n\nHere is how the family\'s itinerary would flow, powered by ManipurApp:\n\n#### **Day 1: Imphal Cultural & Heritage Tour (Ease into the Culture)**\n*   **Morning: Arrival & Hotel Check-in**\n    *   *ManipurApp Module Used:* **Taxi Module.** The family books a pre-vetted airport taxi to their hotel.\n*   **Afternoon: Kangla Fort & Kangla Museum** \n    *   *ManipurApp Module Used:* **Tourism Module.** They can book a certified local tour guide through the app to explain the rich history of the Meitei rulers.\n*   **Late Afternoon: Ima Keithel (Mother\'s Market)**\n    *   A visit to the world\'s only all-women-run market. \n    *   *ManipurApp Module Used:* **Member Services / Tourism.** Send a push notification guide on \"Etiquette and Souvenir Shopping at Ima Keithel.\"\n*   **Dinner: Authentic Manipuri Fine Dining**\n    *   *ManipurApp Module Used:* **Restaurant Module.** The family books a table at a top-rated traditional restaurant (e.g., Classic Grande’s dining or local heritage eateries) to try a mild, family-friendly version of *Eromba* or local fish dishes.\n\n#### **Day 2: Loktak Lake & Keibul Lamjao National Park (The Nature Highlight)**\n*   **All-Day Excursion (Moirang, Loktak, Keibul Lamjao)**\n    *   *ManipurApp Module Used:* **Taxi / Commercial Vehicle Rental.** Because this trip is about 50 km from Imphal, they will need a comfortable SUV (like an Innova) for the family. They book this the night before via the app\'s Commercial Vehicle/Taxi module.\n*   **Key Experiences:**\n    *   **Keibul Lamjao:** Spotting the rare Sangai (Dancing Deer)—highly engaging for children.\n    *   **Loktak Lake:** Booking a traditional boat ride to see the *Phumdis* (floating islands) and visiting Karang Island.\n    *   **INA Memorial (Moirang):** A patriotic stop where the Netaji Subhash Chandra Bose’s INA first hoisted the Indian flag on mainland soil.\n*   **On-the-Go Comfort:**\n    *   *ManipurApp Module Used:* **Fresh Food/Groceries.** Before leaving the hotel at 8:00 AM, the family can order mineral water, fresh fruits, and local snacks to be delivered to their hotel lobby for the road trip.\n\n#### **Day 3: Crafts, Local Life & Departure**\n*   **Morning: Andro Pottery Village or Kakching Garden**\n    *   *ManipurApp Module Used:* **Tourism / Taxi.** A short morning trip to Andro to witness ancient pot-making heritage and the cultural museum, or a relaxing stroll at Kakching Garden.\n*   **Afternoon: Last-minute Souvenir Shopping & Airport Drop**\n    *   *ManipurApp Module Used:* **Taxi Module.** Reliable, scheduled ride-hailing to ensure they reach the airport on time for their flight back to Delhi.\n    *   *ManipurApp Module Used:* **Member Services.** A post-trip feedback survey is triggered on the app, offering them loyalty points redeemable on their next visit or if they refer a friend.\n\n---\n\n### Administrator’s Action Plan\n\nTo make this a reality on the platform:\n1. **Coordinate with Vendors:** Ensure your registered taxi drivers have clean, air-conditioned vehicles suitable for families.\n2. **Feature the Itinerary:** Banner space on the ManipurApp home screen should feature: *\"Visiting for 3 Days? Here is your perfect family itinerary.\"* Linked directly to the booking modules.\n3. **Safety & Trust:** Highlight that all drivers and guides booked through ManipurApp are verified, as safety is a top priority for travelers coming from Delhi.\n\n*Note: As an AI assistant, I do not have live database access to your current registered taxi fleets, real-time ticket availability for Loktak Lake, or active restaurant table inventories. You will need to verify active vendor listings and set pricing dynamically via your Admin Control Panel.*', 'gemini-3.5-flash', 17979, 'COMPLETED', 'GENERAL', 0, '2026-09-20 17:43:10'),
(2, 1, 1, 'what are some destinations to visit when i reach manipur. this is my first time visiting manipur.', 'Welcome to Manipur! Based on the verified records in the ManipurApp database, here are 5 key destinations you can visit, along with their location, best time to visit, and suggested duration:\n\n### **In and Around Imphal (Capital Area)**\nThese destinations are centrally located in the capital, making them excellent starting points for your first visit:\n\n1. **Kangla Fort**\n   * **Description:** Historic heart of Imphal and an important cultural heritage site.\n   * **Location:** Imphal (Imphal West district)\n   * **Best Time to Visit:** October to March\n   * **Suggested Duration:** 2-3 hours\n\n2. **Shree Govindajee Temple**\n   * **Description:** Historic Vaishnavite temple complex in the heart of Imphal.\n   * **Location:** Imphal (Imphal West district)\n   * **Best Time to Visit:** October to March\n   * **Suggested Duration:** 1-2 hours\n\n### **Bishnupur District (Natural & Wildlife Attractions)**\nLocated in Moirang, these two iconic locations are near each other and make for a perfect combined trip:\n\n3. **Loktak Lake**\n   * **Description:** Manipur\'s iconic freshwater lake and a major nature destination.\n   * **Location:** Moirang (Bishnupur district)\n   * **Best Time to Visit:** October to April\n   * **Suggested Duration:** Half day\n\n4. **Keibul Lamjao National Park**\n   * **Description:** A unique floating national park and habitat of the Sangai deer.\n   * **Location:** Moirang (Bishnupur district)\n   * **Best Time to Visit:** November to March\n   * **Suggested Duration:** Half day\n\n### **Cultural Experiences**\n5. **Andro**\n   * **Description:** A cultural village destination known for traditional heritage, crafts, and local experiences.\n   * **Location:** Andro (Imphal East district)\n   * **Best Time to Visit:** October to March\n   * **Suggested Duration:** Half day\n\n---\n\n### **General Planning Advice (Non-Database Info):**\n* **Suggested Route:** For a first-time visitor, you can spend your first day exploring the historical and cultural sites within Imphal (Kangla Fort and Shree Govindajee Temple). On your second day, you can take a day trip to Bishnupur district to experience Loktak Lake and Keibul Lamjao National Park together. Save Andro for a dedicated half-day cultural excursion.', 'gemini-3.5-flash', 14986, 'COMPLETED', 'DESTINATIONS', 5, '2026-09-20 18:09:26'),
(3, 1, 1, 'Give me destination ideas so that i can visit when i come to manipur. i have only 2 days visiting time.', 'Based on the ManipurApp database, here is a practical 2-day itinerary featuring all 5 of our registered destinations. Since they are grouped geographically, you can easily cover them in two days.\n\n### **Day 1: Imphal City Heritage & Culture (Imphal West & East)**\n*General planning advice: Since these three sites are close to or within Imphal, they can be easily combined on your first day.*\n\n*   **Kangla Fort** (ID: 2)\n    *   **Description:** Historic heart of Imphal and an important cultural heritage site.\n    *   **Location:** Imphal (Imphal West district)\n    *   **Suggested Duration:** 2-3 hours\n    *   **Best Time to Visit:** October to March\n*   **Shree Govindajee Temple** (ID: 5)\n    *   **Description:** Historic Vaishnavite temple complex in the heart of Imphal.\n    *   **Location:** Imphal (Imphal West district)\n    *   **Suggested Duration:** 1-2 hours\n    *   **Best Time to Visit:** October to March\n*   **Andro** (ID: 4)\n    *   **Description:** A cultural village destination known for traditional heritage, crafts, and local experiences.\n    *   **Location:** Andro (Imphal East district)\n    *   **Suggested Duration:** Half day\n    *   **Best Time to Visit:** October to March\n\n---\n\n### **Day 2: Nature & Wildlife of Moirang (Bishnupur District)**\n*General planning advice: These two iconic natural spots are located in the same area (Moirang, Bishnupur district) and make a perfect nature-focused day trip.*\n\n*   **Loktak Lake** (ID: 1)\n    *   **Description:** Manipur\'s iconic freshwater lake and a major nature destination.\n    *   **Location:** Moirang (Bishnupur district)\n    *   **Suggested Duration:** Half day\n    *   **Best Time to Visit:** October to April\n*   **Keibul Lamjao National Park** (ID: 3)\n    *   **Description:** A unique floating national park and habitat of the Sangai deer.\n    *   **Location:** Moirang (Bishnupur district)\n    *   **Suggested Duration:** Half day\n    *   **Best Time to Visit:** November to March', 'gemini-3.5-flash', 20054, 'COMPLETED', 'DESTINATIONS', 5, '2026-09-20 18:28:09'),
(4, 1, 1, 'give me atleast 2 destinations , im visiting manipur this winter.', 'Based on the ManipurApp database, here are three excellent destinations to visit during the winter season, matching your travel window:\n\n### 1. Loktak Lake\n*   **District/City:** Bishnupur, Moirang\n*   **Best Time to Visit:** October to April\n*   **Suggested Duration:** Half day\n*   **Description:** Manipur\'s iconic freshwater lake and a major nature destination.\n\n### 2. Keibul Lamjao National Park\n*   **District/City:** Bishnupur, Moirang\n*   **Best Time to Visit:** November to March\n*   **Suggested Duration:** Half day\n*   **Description:** A unique floating national park and habitat of the Sangai deer. \n\n### 3. Kangla Fort\n*   **District/City:** Imphal West, Imphal\n*   **Best Time to Visit:** October to March\n*   **Suggested Duration:** 2-3 hours\n*   **Description:** Historic heart of Imphal and an important cultural heritage site.\n\n*(Note: Since Loktak Lake and Keibul Lamjao National Park are both located in the Bishnupur/Moirang area, they can easily be combined into a single day-trip itinerary).*', 'gemini-3.5-flash', 15027, 'COMPLETED', 'DESTINATIONS', 5, '2026-09-20 18:42:48'),
(5, 1, 1, 'i need some best places to stay in ukhrul. im visiting imphal next weekend.', '### **Ukhrul Accommodations**\n**No matching records were found in the selected ManipurApp category (STAYS) for Ukhrul.** \n\n* **General Planning Advice (Not database-backed):** Generally, travelers to Ukhrul look for local homestays, basic guest houses, or budget hotels around the main Ukhrul town or near scenic areas like Phangrei and Shirui Village. Since these are not registered in our database yet, we recommend checking local travel directories or booking directly with local operators upon arrival.\n\n---\n\n### **Imphal Accommodations (Database-Backed)**\nSince you mentioned you are visiting **Imphal** next weekend, here are the verified options available in the ManipurApp database for both **Imphal East** and **Imphal West**. \n\n*(Note: These are currently active test listings in the database).*\n\n#### **Imphal East Options:**\n1. **[TEST] Imphal East Hotel 1** (HOTEL)\n   * **Starting Price:** 1850.00 per night for a Standard Room (Queen Bed, max 2 guests).\n   * **Amenities:** Wi-Fi, Parking, Hot Water, Breakfast.\n2. **[TEST] Imphal East Lodge 2** (LODGE)\n   * **Starting Price:** 2200.00 per night for a Standard Room (Queen Bed, max 2 guests).\n   * **Amenities:** Wi-Fi, Parking, Hot Water, Breakfast.\n3. **[TEST] Imphal East Homestay 3** (HOMESTAY)\n   * **Starting Price:** 2550.00 per night for a Standard Room (Queen Bed, max 2 guests).\n   * **Amenities:** Wi-Fi, Parking, Hot Water, Breakfast.\n4. **[TEST] Imphal East Guest House 4** (GUEST_HOUSE)\n   * **Starting Price:** 2900.00 per night for a Standard Room (Queen Bed, max 2 guests).\n   * **Amenities:** Wi-Fi, Parking, Hot Water, Breakfast.\n5. **[TEST] Imphal East Resort 5** (RESORT)\n   * **Starting Price:** 3250.00 per night for a Standard Room (Queen Bed, max 2 guests).\n   * **Amenities:** Wi-Fi, Parking, Hot Water, Breakfast.\n\n#### **Imphal West Options:**\n1. **[TEST] Imphal West Hotel 1** (HOTEL)\n   * **Starting Price:** 1850.00 per night for a Standard Room (Queen Bed, max 2 guests).\n   * **Amenities:** Wi-Fi, Parking, Hot Water, Breakfast.\n2. **[TEST] Imphal West Lodge 2** (LODGE)\n   * **Starting Price:** 2200.00 per night for a Standard Room (Queen Bed, max 2 guests).\n   * **Amenities:** Wi-Fi, Parking, Hot Water, Breakfast.\n3. **[TEST] Imphal West Homestay 3** (HOMESTAY)\n   * **Starting Price:** 2550.00 per night for a Standard Room (Queen Bed, max 2 guests).\n   * **Amenities:** Wi-Fi, Parking, Hot Water, Breakfast.\n4. **[TEST] Imphal West Guest House 4** (GUEST_HOUSE)\n   * **Starting Price:** 2900.00 per night for a Standard Room (Queen Bed, max 2 guests).\n   * **Amenities:** Wi-Fi, Parking, Hot Water, Breakfast.\n5. **[TEST] Imphal West Resort 5** (RESORT)\n   * **Starting Price:** 3250.00 per night for a Standard Room (Queen Bed, max 2 guests).\n   * **Amenities:** Wi-Fi, Parking, Hot Water, Breakfast.', 'gemini-3.5-flash', 18040, 'COMPLETED', 'STAYS', 25, '2026-09-20 18:53:29'),
(6, 1, 1, 'ok give me where to stay in chandel', 'Based on the ManipurApp database context for **STAYS**, there are 5 records found for the **Chandel** district. \n\n*Please note: As indicated in the database description, all of these listings are synthetic records created for testing the tourism module and do not represent real physical property listings.*\n\nHere are the details of the test stays in Chandel:\n\n### 1. [TEST] Chandel Hotel 1 (HOTEL)\n*   **Starting Price:** 1850.00 per night\n*   **Amenities:** Wi-Fi, Parking, Hot Water, Breakfast\n*   **Room Types:** \n    *   *Standard Room:* Queen Bed, max 2 guests (Price: 1850.00 per night)\n\n### 2. [TEST] Chandel Lodge 2 (LODGE)\n*   **Starting Price:** 2200.00 per night\n*   **Amenities:** Wi-Fi, Parking, Hot Water, Breakfast\n*   **Room Types:** \n    *   *Standard Room:* Queen Bed, max 2 guests (Price: 2200.00 per night)\n\n### 3. [TEST] Chandel Homestay 3 (HOMESTAY)\n*   **Starting Price:** 2550.00 per night\n*   **Amenities:** Wi-Fi, Parking, Hot Water, Breakfast\n*   **Room Types:** \n    *   *Standard Room:* Queen Bed, max 2 guests (Price: 2550.00 per night)\n\n### 4. [TEST] Chandel Guest House 4 (GUEST_HOUSE)\n*   **Starting Price:** 2900.00 per night\n*   **Amenities:** Wi-Fi, Parking, Hot Water, Breakfast\n*   **Room Types:** \n    *   *Standard Room:* Queen Bed, max 2 guests (Price: 2900.00 per night)\n\n### 5. [TEST] Chandel Resort 5 (RESORT)\n*   **Starting Price:** 3250.00 per night\n*   **Amenities:** Wi-Fi, Parking, Hot Water, Breakfast\n*   **Room Types:** \n    *   *Standard Room:* Queen Bed, max 2 guests (Price: 3250.00 per night)\n\n---\n\n### General Planning Advice:\nBecause the currently listed database options for Chandel are synthetic test records, you will need to look beyond the live database for actual bookings. When planning a real trip to Chandel:\n*   Accommodations are typically limited to government guest houses, local homestays, or budget lodges.\n*   It is highly recommended to contact local tourism offices in Manipur or travel coordinators in Imphal to arrange verified homestays or guest house bookings in Chandel before departing.', 'gemini-3.5-flash', 18193, 'COMPLETED', 'STAYS', 25, '2026-09-20 18:55:31'),
(7, 1, 1, 'ok give me where to stay in Ukhrul', 'No matching records were found in the selected ManipurApp category (STAYS) for **Ukhrul**. The current database only contains test listings for Bishnupur, Chandel, Churachandpur, Imphal East, and Imphal West.\n\n### General Planning Advice (Not database-backed):\nIf you are planning a visit to Ukhrul, here is some general travel information to assist you:\n* **Types of Stays:** Ukhrul town offers various local homestays, budget hotels, and government guest houses. Staying at a local homestay is highly recommended to experience Tangkhul Naga hospitality and local cuisine.\n* **Key Areas:** Look for accommodations near Ukhrul Town center for easy access to transport, or closer to Shirui Village if you are planning to trek Shirui Kashong Peak.\n* **Booking Tip:** Because these options are not currently registered in the database, it is best to contact local tour operators in Manipur or check trusted regional travel directories to book these stays in advance.', 'gemini-3.5-flash', 14471, 'COMPLETED', 'STAYS', 25, '2026-09-20 18:56:01'),
(8, 1, 1, 'suggest some tour packages for manipur', 'Based on the ManipurApp database, here are the available tour packages for Manipur:\n\n### 1. **Loktak & Sangai Escape - 2 Days**\n* **Description:** A sample nature-focused itinerary around Loktak Lake and Keibul Lamjao National Park.\n* **Duration:** 2 Days, 1 Night\n* **Pricing:** \n  * Base Price: **7500.00 INR** per person\n  * Discounted Price: **6499.00 INR** per person\n* **Max Travellers:** 6\n* **Destinations Included:**\n  * **Day 1:** Loktak Lake (Moirang, Bishnupur), Kangla Fort (Imphal, Imphal West), and Shree Govindajee Temple (Imphal, Imphal West).\n  * **Day 2:** Keibul Lamjao National Park (Moirang, Bishnupur).\n  * **Day 3:** Andro (Andro, Imphal East).\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Manipur Highlights - 3 Days**\n* **Description:** A sample development package connecting Imphal, Kangla Fort, Loktak Lake, Moirang, and Keibul Lamjao.\n* **Duration:** 3 Days, 2 Nights\n* **Pricing:** \n  * Base Price: **12000.00 INR** per person\n  * Discounted Price: **9999.00 INR** per person\n* **Max Travellers:** 6\n* **Destinations Included:**\n  * **Day 1:** Kangla Fort (Imphal, Imphal West) - Arrival and Imphal heritage visit.\n  * **Day 2:** Loktak Lake (Moirang, Bishnupur) - Lake and Moirang sightseeing.\n  * **Day 3:** Keibul Lamjao National Park (Moirang, Bishnupur) - Floating national park visit.\n\n*(Note: These are sample/development packages currently configured in the ManipurApp administration portal.)*', 'gemini-3.5-flash', 13765, 'COMPLETED', 'PACKAGES', 2, '2026-09-20 18:59:28'),
(9, 1, 1, 'find me some good places to stay in ukhrul. im visiting next week.', 'Based on the ManipurApp database context for the **STAYS** category, there are 5 records found for Ukhrul. Please note that all currently available records are **synthetic test listings** created for Tourism module testing and are not real property listings. \n\nHere are the details of the test stays recorded in the database:\n\n1. **[TEST] Ukhrul Hotel 1** (HOTEL)\n   * **Starting Price:** 1850.00 per night (Standard Room: 1850.00 per night for a Queen Bed, max 2 guests)\n   * **Amenities:** Wi-Fi, Parking, Hot Water, Breakfast\n   * **Address:** Test tourism address, Ukhrul\n\n2. **[TEST] Ukhrul Lodge 2** (LODGE)\n   * **Starting Price:** 2200.00 per night (Standard Room: 2200.00 per night for a Queen Bed, max 2 guests)\n   * **Amenities:** Wi-Fi, Parking, Hot Water, Breakfast\n   * **Address:** Test tourism address, Ukhrul\n\n3. **[TEST] Ukhrul Homestay 3** (HOMESTAY)\n   * **Starting Price:** 2550.00 per night (Standard Room: 2550.00 per night for a Queen Bed, max 2 guests)\n   * **Amenities:** Wi-Fi, Parking, Hot Water, Breakfast\n   * **Address:** Test tourism address, Ukhrul\n\n4. **[TEST] Ukhrul Guest House 4** (GUEST_HOUSE)\n   * **Starting Price:** 2900.00 per night (Standard Room: 2900.00 per night for a Queen Bed, max 2 guests)\n   * **Amenities:** Wi-Fi, Parking, Hot Water, Breakfast\n   * **Address:** Test tourism address, Ukhrul\n\n5. **[TEST] Ukhrul Resort 5** (RESORT)\n   * **Starting Price:** 3250.00 per night (Standard Room: 3250.00 per night for a Queen Bed, max 2 guests)\n   * **Amenities:** Wi-Fi, Parking, Hot Water, Breakfast\n   * **Address:** Test tourism address, Ukhrul\n\n---\n**General Planning Advice:**\nSince the database currently only contains synthetic test records, these properties cannot be booked for your visit next week. For a real trip to Ukhrul, it is recommended to search for verified local homestays or contact the Manipur Tourism department directly to find active, real-world accommodations.', 'gemini-3.5-flash', 17796, 'COMPLETED', 'STAYS', 5, '2026-09-20 19:09:50'),
(10, 1, 1, 'get me non veg restaurant where i can have food in imphdal', 'Based on the ManipurApp database, here are the restaurants in Imphal that serve non-vegetarian food, along with their locations and non-veg menu options:\n\n### 1. **Ema Kitchen**\n*   **Location:** Paona Bazaar, Imphal (Imphal West)\n*   **Non-Veg Menu Items:**\n    *   *Eromba* (Mashed vegetables with fermented fish): 160.00\n    *   *Ngari Eromba* (Fermented fish and vegetable dish): 220.00\n    *   *Chicken Noodles*: 220.00\n    *   *Chicken Curry*: 280.00\n    *   *Chicken Kangou*: 300.00\n    *   *Manipuri Chicken Thali*: 320.00\n    *   *Chicken Thali*: 350.00\n*   **Order Details:** Minimum order of 150.00. Delivery fee is 30.00 (free delivery above 500.00). Delivery and pickup available.\n\n### 2. **Hillside Café**\n*   **Location:** Uripok, Imphal (Imphal West)\n*   **Non-Veg Menu Items:**\n    *   *Masala Omelette*: 110.00\n    *   *Chicken Sandwich*: 190.00\n    *   *Chicken Rice Bowl*: 260.00\n    *   *Chicken Alfredo Pasta*: 290.00\n*   **Order Details:** Minimum order of 120.00. Delivery fee is 25.00 (free delivery above 400.00). Delivery and pickup available.\n\n### 3. **Imphal Kitchen**\n*   **Location:** MG Avenue, Imphal (Imphal West)\n*   **Non-Veg Menu Items:**\n    *   *Chicken Curry*: 280.00\n    *   *Chicken Biryani*: 300.00\n    *   *Butter Chicken*: 320.00\n*   **Order Details:** Minimum order of 100.00. Delivery fee is 40.00 (free delivery above 500.00). Delivery and pickup available.\n\n### 4. **Imphal Spice House**\n*   **Location:** Sangakpham, Imphal (Imphal East)\n*   **Non-Veg Menu Items:**\n    *   *Chicken Hakka Noodles*: 230.00\n    *   *Chicken 65*: 260.00\n    *   *Chicken Biryani*: 300.00\n    *   *Butter Chicken*: 330.00\n*   **Order Details:** Minimum order of 150.00. Delivery fee is 35.00 (free delivery above 500.00). Delivery and pickup available.\n\n### 5. **Tribal Foods**\n*   **Location:** Porompat, Imphal (Imphal East)\n*   **Non-Veg Menu Items:**\n    *   *Smoked Chicken*: 320.00\n    *   *Smoked Pork Rice Bowl*: 340.00\n    *   *Smoked Pork Curry*: 360.00\n    *   *Pork with Bamboo Shoot*: 380.00\n*   **Order Details:** Minimum order of 180.00. Delivery fee is 40.00 (free delivery above 600.00). Delivery and pickup available.\n\n### 6. **Yaiphaba Kitchen**\n*   **Location:** Keishampat, Imphal (Imphal West)\n*   **Non-Veg Menu Items:**\n    *   *Chicken Masala*: 290.00\n    *   *Chicken Biryani*: 310.00\n    *   *Chicken Thali*: 330.00\n    *   *Special Chicken Thali*: 420.00\n*   **Order Details:** Minimum order of 200.00. Delivery fee is 35.00 (free delivery above 550.00). Delivery and pickup available.', 'gemini-3.5-flash', 14599, 'COMPLETED', 'RESTAURANTS', 6, '2026-09-20 19:37:26'),
(11, 1, 1, 'suggest any food to order-im hungry, i have only 100 rs', 'Based on the ManipurApp database, here are the food and beverage options priced at **₹100 or less**. \n\nPlease note that **minimum order amounts** and **delivery fees** apply for delivery orders, which may require a higher budget or multiple items to place the order.\n\n### **Snacks & Desserts (₹100)**\n* **French Fries** \n  * **Price:** ₹100.00\n  * **Restaurant:** Chingol Café (Bishnupur)\n  * *Note:* Minimum order is ₹100.00; Delivery fee is ₹20.00.\n* **Gulab Jamun** \n  * **Price:** ₹100.00\n  * **Restaurants:** \n    * Chingol Café (Bishnupur) — *Minimum order: ₹100.00, Delivery fee: ₹20.00*\n    * Imphal Kitchen (Imphal West) — *Minimum order: ₹100.00, Delivery fee: ₹40.00*\n\n---\n\n### **Drinks & Beverages (Under ₹100)**\nIf you want to combine items or order multiples to meet minimum order limits:\n\n* **Fresh Lime Soda**\n  * **Price:** ₹80.00\n  * **Restaurants:**\n    * Imphal Kitchen — *Minimum order: ₹100.00, Delivery fee: ₹40.00*\n    * Ema Kitchen — *Minimum order: ₹150.00, Delivery fee: ₹30.00*\n    * Imphal Spice House — *Minimum order: ₹150.00, Delivery fee: ₹35.00*\n* **Lemon Tea**\n  * **Price:** ₹60.00\n  * **Restaurant:** Tribal Foods (Imphal East)\n  * *Note:* Minimum order is ₹180.00.\n* **Masala Tea**\n  * **Price:** ₹50.00 \n  * **Restaurants:**\n    * Chingol Café — *Minimum order: ₹100.00 (Tip: You can order 2 Masala Teas to hit exactly ₹100 for food!)*\n    * Imphal Kitchen — *Minimum order: ₹100.00*\n* **Black Tea**\n  * **Price:** ₹40.00\n  * **Restaurant:** Ema Kitchen (Imphal West)\n  * *Note:* Minimum order is ₹150.00.', 'gemini-3.5-flash', 14061, 'COMPLETED', 'RESTAURANT_MENU', 50, '2026-09-20 19:38:33'),
(12, 1, 1, 'any vegetarian restaurant nearby classic hotel imphal', 'Based on the ManipurApp database, there are no restaurants explicitly listed as being located directly next to or at \"Classic Hotel Imphal\". \n\nHowever, there are several restaurants in Imphal registered on the platform that offer vegetarian options. Since they all support delivery and pickup, they may be able to service your location:\n\n### 1. Ema Kitchen\n*   **Location:** Paona Bazaar, Imphal West\n*   **Vegetarian Options:** \n    *   *Veg Thali* (Vegetarian meal with rice, dal, vegetables, and sides) – **₹280.00**\n*   **Delivery Details:** Delivery available for a fee of **₹30.00** (Free delivery on orders above **₹500.00**). Minimum order amount is **₹150.00**.\n\n### 2. Yaiphaba Kitchen\n*   **Location:** Keishampat, Imphal West\n*   **Vegetarian Options:**\n    *   *Veg Thali* (Complete vegetarian meal with rice, dal, and seasonal sides) – **₹240.00**\n    *   *Dal Tadka* (Yellow lentils tempered with spices) – **₹160.00**\n    *   *Mixed Veg Curry* (Seasonal vegetables in mild gravy) – **₹190.00**\n*   **Delivery Details:** Delivery available for a fee of **₹35.00** (Free delivery on orders above **₹550.00**). Minimum order amount is **₹200.00**.\n\n### 3. Tribal Foods\n*   **Location:** Porompat, Imphal East\n*   **Vegetarian Options:**\n    *   *Champhut* (Simple seasonal vegetable preparation) – **₹140.00**\n    *   *Kanghou* (Stir-fried local vegetables with herbs) – **₹170.00**\n*   **Delivery Details:** Delivery available for a fee of **₹40.00** (Free delivery on orders above **₹600.00**). Minimum order amount is **₹180.00**.\n\n---\n*Disclaimer / General Advice: Locally, Classic Hotel Imphal is located around the North A.O.C. area. Paona Bazaar, Keishampat, and Porompat are nearby commercial areas within Imphal (typically a 5 to 15-minute drive depending on traffic). Ordering via the delivery options listed above is highly practical for these distances.*', 'gemini-3.5-flash', 14455, 'COMPLETED', 'RESTAURANTS', 3, '2026-09-20 19:40:11'),
(13, 1, 1, 'any vegetarian restaurant nearby classic hotel imphal', 'Based on the ManipurApp database context, there are no restaurant records that explicitly mention \"Classic Hotel Imphal\" or their exact distance from it. \n\nHowever, there are three restaurants in the Imphal area with registered vegetarian options. Below are their database details, including their locations and vegetarian menus:\n\n### 1. Ema Kitchen\n*   **Location:** Paona Bazaar, Imphal West (postal code: 795001)\n*   **Cuisine:** Manipuri, Indian\n*   **Vegetarian Menu Items:**\n    *   **Veg Thali:** ₹280.00 (Vegetarian meal with rice, dal, vegetables, and sides)\n*   **Delivery Details:** Delivery available for a fee of ₹30.00 (free delivery for orders above ₹500.00; minimum order amount is ₹150.00).\n\n### 2. Yaiphaba Kitchen\n*   **Location:** Keishampat, Imphal West\n*   **Cuisine:** Manipuri, Indian, Thali\n*   **Vegetarian Menu Items:**\n    *   **Veg Thali:** ₹240.00 (Complete vegetarian meal with rice, dal, and seasonal sides)\n    *   **Dal Tadka:** ₹160.00 (Yellow lentils tempered with spices)\n    *   **Mixed Veg Curry:** ₹190.00 (Seasonal vegetables in mild gravy)\n*   **Delivery Details:** Delivery available for a fee of ₹35.00 (free delivery for orders above ₹550.00; minimum order amount is ₹200.00).\n\n### 3. Tribal Foods\n*   **Location:** Porompat, Imphal East\n*   **Cuisine:** Northeast Indian, Manipuri\n*   **Vegetarian Menu Items:**\n    *   **Champhut:** ₹140.00 (Simple seasonal vegetable preparation)\n    *   **Kanghou:** ₹170.00 (Stir-fried local vegetables with herbs)\n*   **Delivery Details:** Delivery available for a fee of ₹40.00 (free delivery for orders above ₹600.00; minimum order amount is ₹180.00).\n\n***\n\n**General Planning Advice (Non-Database Fact):**\nGeographically, The Classic Hotel is located at North AOC in Imphal. Out of the options above, Paona Bazaar (Ema Kitchen) and Keishampat (Yaiphaba Kitchen) are located in Imphal West, while Porompat (Tribal Foods) is in Imphal East. Depending on local traffic, all three locations are relatively close to North AOC for delivery or pickup.', 'gemini-3.5-flash', 16182, 'COMPLETED', 'RESTAURANTS', 3, '2026-09-20 19:45:37'),
(14, 1, 16, 'Help me with my Manipur trip plan. Help me plan a trip in Manipur.', 'Hello! As the ManipurApp AI for the platform administrator, I can help you with your trip planning using the available database overview.\n\n### ManipurApp Database Overview (Tourism Category)\nAccording to the live database summary, we currently have the following records available:\n*   **Destinations:** 5\n*   **Stays:** 80\n*   **Packages:** 2\n*   **Guides:** 2\n*   **Experiences:** 1\n*   **Events:** 2\n\n*Note: No specific, detailed records (such as names, prices, or exact locations of these stays, packages, or guides) were returned in the current database context. To book or view specific options, please query those individual categories directly.*\n\n---\n\n### General Manipur Trip Planning Advice\n*(Please note: The following is general travel planning advice and is not pulled from specific ManipurApp database records.)*\n\nIf you are planning a trip to Manipur, here is a general way to structure a 4 to 5-day itinerary:\n\n*   **Day 1: Imphal (Arrival & Culture)**\n    *   Explore **Kangla Fort**, the ancient seat of Manipur\'s rulers.\n    *   Visit the famous **Ima Keithel (Mother\'s Market)**, an all-women-run market.\n*   **Day 2: Loktak Lake & Wildlife**\n    *   Take a day trip to **Loktak Lake**, the largest freshwater lake in Northeast India, famous for its floating islands (*phumdis*).\n    *   Visit the **Keibul Lamjao National Park**, the world\'s only floating national park and home to the endangered Sangai (brow-antlered deer).\n*   **Day 3: History & Borders (Moreh)**\n    *   Consider a trip to the border town of **Moreh** (if travel permissions and local conditions permit) for a unique cross-border market experience.\n*   **Day 4: Scenic Hills (Ukhrul or Senapati)**\n    *   Travel to **Ukhrul** to experience the beautiful Shirui Hills and local Tangkhul Naga culture.\n\n**Best Time to Visit:** Between October and April, when the weather is pleasant and ideal for sightseeing. \n\nIf you need specific details on the 80 stays, 2 packages, or 2 guides registered on the platform, please request a database pull for those specific record types!', 'gemini-3.5-flash', 12868, 'COMPLETED', 'TOURISM', 92, '2026-09-20 20:02:50'),
(15, 1, 16, 'Help me with my Manipur trip plan. Help me plan a trip in Manipur.', 'Based on the current database context for the **TOURISM** category, here is the status of your query:\n\n### 📊 ManipurApp Database Summary\nWhile we have high-level counts of registered tourism services on the platform, **no individual detailed records** (such as specific names, pricing, or locations) were returned in the active database context. \n\n*   **Registered Destinations:** 5\n*   **Registered Stays:** 80\n*   **Active Packages:** 2\n*   **Available Guides:** 2\n*   **Experiences:** 1\n*   **Upcoming Events:** 2\n\n*Note: Since the detailed records list is currently empty (`\"records\": []`), no specific database-backed destinations, stays, packages, or guides can be verified or recommended at this moment.*\n\n---\n\n### 🗺️ General Manipur Planning Advice\n*(Please note: The following recommendations are general travel advice and are not retrieved from the live ManipurApp database records.)*\n\nIf you are planning a trip to Manipur, here is a standard recommended itinerary layout:\n\n1.  **Imphal (Capital City):** \n    *   *What to see:* Kangla Fort, Ima Keithel (all-women\'s market), and the Manipur State Museum.\n    *   *Duration:* 1–2 days.\n2.  **Moirang & Loktak Lake:** \n    *   *What to see:* Loktak Lake (the largest freshwater lake in Northeast India) and the floating phumdis. Visit Sendra Island and the Keibul Lamjao National Park (the world\'s only floating national park, home to the Sangai deer).\n    *   *Duration:* 1–2 days.\n3.  **Ukhrul (Hill Station):** \n    *   *What to see:* Shirui Kashong Peak (famous for the Shirui Lily) and Khangkhui Mangsor Cave.\n    *   *Duration:* 2 days.\n\n**Best Time to Visit:** Between October and April for pleasant weather and local festivals like the Sangai Festival (usually held in November).', 'gemini-3.5-flash', 13732, 'COMPLETED', 'TOURISM', 92, '2026-09-20 20:03:04'),
(16, 1, 16, 'About this destination: Kangla Fort. What are the best things to see here?', 'Based on the ManipurApp database context, here is the official record for this destination:\n\n* **Name:** Kangla Fort (ID: 2)\n* **Location:** Imphal, Imphal West District\n* **Database Description:** \"Historic heart of Imphal and an important cultural heritage site.\"\n* **Best Time to Visit:** October to March\n* **Suggested Duration:** 2-3 hours\n\n### Sights and Points of Interest\nThe ManipurApp database record for Kangla Fort **does not contain a list of specific attractions or sights** within the fort grounds. \n\n**General Planning Advice (Non-Database Information):**\nFor visitors planning to spend the suggested 2-3 hours there, prominent historical and cultural features typically visited inside the Kangla Fort complex include:\n* **The Kangla Sha:** The majestic plaster statues of the state emblem (half-lion, half-dragon creatures) which were historically destroyed but have been reconstructed.\n* **The Govindajee Temple:** A historic temple structure located within the fort enclave.\n* **The Ruins of the Royal Palace & Coronation Site (Uttra):** The historical seat of power for the rulers of Manipur.\n* **Kangla Museum:** Displays historical maps, portraits of kings, and artifacts detailing the history of the fort and the kingdom.\n* **The Inner Moat:** The scenic waterways surrounding the fort area.', 'gemini-3.5-flash', 17193, 'COMPLETED', 'DESTINATIONS', 1, '2026-09-20 20:04:28'),
(17, 1, 16, 'What are the best things to see here?', 'Based on the ManipurApp database, here are the top destinations to see:\n\n1. **Loktak Lake**\n   * **Description:** Manipur\'s iconic freshwater lake and a major nature destination.\n   * **Location:** Moirang, Bishnupur District\n   * **Best Time to Visit:** October to April\n   * **Suggested Duration:** Half day\n\n2. **Keibul Lamjao National Park**\n   * **Description:** A unique floating national park and habitat of the Sangai deer.\n   * **Location:** Moirang, Bishnupur District\n   * **Best Time to Visit:** November to March\n   * **Suggested Duration:** Half day\n\n3. **Kangla Fort**\n   * **Description:** Historic heart of Imphal and an important cultural heritage site.\n   * **Location:** Imphal, Imphal West District\n   * **Best Time to Visit:** October to March\n   * **Suggested Duration:** 2-3 hours\n\n4. **Andro**\n   * **Description:** A cultural village destination known for traditional heritage, crafts, and local experiences.\n   * **Location:** Andro, Imphal East District\n   * **Best Time to Visit:** October to March\n   * **Suggested Duration:** Half day\n\n5. **Shree Govindajee Temple**\n   * **Description:** Historic Vaishnavite temple complex in the heart of Imphal.\n   * **Location:** Imphal, Imphal West District\n   * **Best Time to Visit:** October to March\n   * **Suggested Duration:** 1-2 hours', 'gemini-3.5-flash', 9859, 'COMPLETED', 'DESTINATIONS', 5, '2026-09-20 21:40:44'),
(18, 1, 16, 'What can I do in Manipur?', 'Based on the ManipurApp database for the **Tourism** category, here is an overview of what is currently registered on the platform:\n\n*   **Destinations:** 5 registered destinations to visit.\n*   **Stays:** 80 accommodation options available.\n*   **Packages:** 2 curated tour packages.\n*   **Guides:** 2 registered tour guides.\n*   **Experiences:** 1 curated local experience.\n*   **Events:** 2 scheduled events.\n\n*(Note: No individual names or specific details for these records were returned in the current database query).*\n\n---\n\n### General Planning Advice (Not database-backed)\nIf you are planning activities in Manipur, popular options generally include:\n*   **Explore Loktak Lake:** Visit the largest freshwater lake in Northeast India, famous for its floating phumdis (islands) and the Keibul Lamjao National Park (the world\'s only floating national park, home to the endangered Sangai deer).\n*   **Historical & Cultural Sightseeing:** Visit the historic Kangla Fort in Imphal, the RKCS Art Gallery, and the INA Martyr\'s Memorial in Moirang.\n*   **Shop at Ima Keithel:** Experience the unique \"Mother\'s Market\" in Imphal, a historic market run exclusively by thousands of women.\n*   **Eco-Tourism:** Trek through the scenic Dzukou Valley (accessible from the Manipur border) or visit the Shirui Hills in Ukhrul.', 'gemini-3.5-flash', 13821, 'COMPLETED', 'TOURISM', 92, '2026-09-20 21:41:48');
